# UI Testing CI Rules

## Parallel Execution

Split E2E tests across CI shards for faster feedback.

```yaml
# GitHub Actions — Playwright sharding
- name: Run Playwright tests
  run: npx playwright test --shard=${{ matrix.shard }}/${{ strategy.job-count }}
  strategy:
    matrix:
      shard: [1, 2, 3, 4]
```

- Minimum 2 shards for any project with E2E tests
- Component tests in a separate job (fast, no sharding needed)
- Unit tests first, E2E in parallel (fail-fast: unit gate)

## Retry Strategy

| Test Type | Retries (CI) | Retries (Local) | Cap |
|-----------|-------------|-----------------|-----|
| E2E | 2 | 0 | Retry rate < 5% total |
| Component | 0 | 0 | N/A |
| Visual Regression | 1 | 0 | Manual verify on diff |

```typescript
// playwright.config.ts
retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0,
```

Track retry rate. If >5% of CI runs trigger retries, stop and investigate flakiness before adding more tests.

## Artifact Management

On failure, ALWAYS persist diagnostic artifacts.

```yaml
- uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
  if: failure()
  with:
    name: playwright-artifacts-${{ matrix.shard }}
    path: |
      test-results/
      playwright-report/
    retention-days: 7
```

- E2E: screenshots + traces (configured in `playwright.config.ts`)
- Component: coverage report on failure (re-run with `--coverage`)
- Retention: max 7 days for CI artifacts

## Coverage Gate

Fail CI if coverage drops below threshold.

```typescript
// vitest.config.ts
test: {
  coverage: {
    thresholds: {
      lines: 80,
      branches: 80,
      functions: 80,
      statements: 80,
    },
  },
}
```

- Gate applies to the full project, not per-file
- If coverage legitimately drops (deleting dead code), adjust threshold consciously — document the change
- Coverage runs in a separate CI step, not as a test gate

## CI Pipeline Layout

```
unit-and-component:    # Fast feedback (~2 min)
  → vitest run --coverage
  → coverage gate check

e2e:                   # Slower, parallelized (~10 min total)
  → start dev server
  → playwright test (sharded 4x)
  → upload artifacts on failure

visual-regression:     # Optional, separate workflow
  → start dev server
  → percy/chromatic snapshot
  → upload diffs

accessibility:         # Optional, weekly or on-demand
  → start dev server
  → axe-core scan
  → report violations
```

Separate workflows allow independent retries and failure notifications.
